filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue grew only 2.6% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841925/000119312526215104/0001193125-26-215104-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-215104"},{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 34.2% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841925/000119312526215104/0001193125-26-215104-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-215104"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 41.7% to 38.0% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001841925"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-70.1% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841925/000119312526215104/0001193125-26-215104-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-215104"},{"text":"About 22 months of cash at the current burn ($174.4m against $93.4m a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841925/000119312526215104/0001193125-26-215104-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-215104"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 8.1% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841925/000119312526215104/0001193125-26-215104-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-215104"},{"text":"Debt of $404.6m against equity of $324.6m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841925/000119312526215104/0001193125-26-215104-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-215104"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 32.2% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (612,133 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841925/000119312526324439/0001193125-26-324439-index.htm"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 30.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.3,"consecutive":2,"current":0.38,"current_display":"38.0%","threshold_display":"30.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -12.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.12,"consecutive":2,"current":0.026,"current_display":"2.6%","threshold_display":"-12.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":22.42,"current_display":"22 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 15.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.15,"consecutive":1,"current":0.081,"